case2.rea
-3                      spatial dimension  ( < 0 --> generate .rea/.re2 pair)
1                       number of fields
#=======================================================================
#
#  term_demo_case2 -- Shaver et al. (Trans. ANS 116, 2017) second test case.
#  "1D via 2D rectangular mesh": inlet/outlet normal to the flow (x), SYM on
#  the two long sides (y), single periodic layer (z) to keep it a thin 3D
#  box standing in for a 2D case. Nondimensional domain length = 1 (paper's
#  z-coordinate maps to this mesh's x). 40 streamwise elements (vs case1's
#  20) since alpha/velocity genuinely evolve from inlet to fully-developed
#  state here and need resolving.
#
#  Letter codes alone do NOT by themselves become real boundary IDs for
#  nekRS's boundaryTypeMap dispatch -- case2.usr's usrdat2() assigns
#  boundaryID explicitly from cbc (same pattern as examples/gabls1,
#  examples/lowMach). West/east use "v"/"O" (unambiguous: these letters are
#  NEVER written by genbox for genuine internal element-element connections,
#  unlike "E" -- see below). South/north use "SYM". Bottom/top are coded "E"
#  and overridden to 'P' in usrdat2 for the single periodic z layer; "E" is
#  safe there ONLY because nelz=1 (no other element in z to be ambiguous
#  with -- every element's bottom/top face is already a true domain
#  boundary). IMPORTANT, found the hard way: do NOT use "E" for west/east
#  here (as this repo's term_demo_case1/case1.usr currently does) -- with
#  nelx=40 (>1), "E" is the SAME code genbox writes for the genuine internal
#  connections between consecutive x-elements, so "ifc==1 .and. cbc=='E  '"
#  matches EVERY element's west face, not just the true boundary one, and
#  boundaryID ends up never set to 1 anywhere (confirmed by re-running
#  case1_v2 in this same session: identical "boundary ID needs to be
#  one-based index but min(ID) is 2!" abort). "v"/"O"/"SYM" are written by
#  genbox ONLY where the .box file's bc line puts them, so matching on cbc
#  value alone (no face-index/position guard needed) is unambiguous.
#
#=======================================================================
#
Box
-40  -1  -1                                           nelx,nely,nelz for Box
0  1  1.                                              x0,x1,gain
0  0.1  1.                                             y0,y1,gain
0  0.1  1.                                             z0,z1,gain
v  ,O  ,SYM,SYM,E  ,E                                  bc's (3 chars each!)
